selected.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve. Production pixel-art desktop girl sprite atlas, EIGHT genuinely distinct consecutive running poses.
Input1 original reference: exact character identity. Input2 existing side-running atlas: match this 45-degree LEFT three-quarter view, style, outfit and moderate lean, but replace the 4-frame cycle with 8 frames.
Layout: FOUR columns by TWO rows, equal cells, wide 2:1 canvas. Exactly 8 full-body sprites, row-major chronological cycle. Transparent background throughout, no floor, no grid lines, no labels, no text. Ample padding. Same head size and pelvis position every cell, same scale, shoes never cropped.
Girl: long straight black hair, large round black glasses, navy jacket with white trim and white shirt, loose patched light-blue jeans, white sneakers. Match original face, glasses, bangs, jacket and patches consistently. Head/chest/hips/shoes face diagonally LEFT, NOT frontal marching. Hair trails gently right.
Create a coherent complete eight-phase run with physically distinct foot contacts:
1 near leg forward contact, far leg trailing;
2 near leg bears weight, torso slightly lowers, far heel curls up;
3 near leg pushes back, far knee passes forward;
4 both feet airborne, far knee lifts forward, near leg extends back;
5 far leg forward contact, near leg trailing (opposite anatomical support from frame1);
6 far leg bears weight, torso slightly lowers, near heel curls up;
7 far leg pushes back, near knee passes forward;
8 both feet airborne, near knee lifts forward ready to return to frame1.
Arms counter-swing and actually change position across phases; keep two legs distinguishable by occlusion, do not repeat same leg or copy same pose. No mirrored alternate-facing frames; ALL face LEFT. Very small 2-4 pixel head bob only, no changing face/head scale. Crisp pixel-art contours matching input. Preserve clothing details and glasses consistently. True transparency.
